        }
      ],
      "notes": "Both formal claims pass entailment checks: Claim 1 (stated tier, M) is a verbatim quote from the policy text accurately characterised; Claim 2 (projected tier, E21) is correctly framed as critics' argument, not asserted as fact. Tier integrity is sound. The direction ('worsens') is plausible given the mechanism \u2014 inflation-uprating embeds a rising barrier to family reunification, with downstream loneliness/belonging effects for diaspora and mixed-nationality households \u2014 and is not false-balanced or lever-leaked. The biggest_unknown appropriately flags the social-trust offset question. The one substantive weakness is the uncited advocacy figure in the rationale (E23/reunitefamiliesuk.co.uk) driving the magnitude assessment without appearing as a formal, labelled claim \u2014 this is a warning, not a blocker, because the overall direction and magnitude ('minor') are still defensible from the surviving formal claims and the MAC evidence referenced. Party-blind check passes; no motive attribution detected."
